{
  "format": 1,
  "side": "client",
  "comment": "Kiln's upscaler swap (0.2.0-dev.29.18 phase B; docs/kiln/graphics.md, native/services/ui/upscale.cpp): the game's FSR 3 upscaler pass on the client (docs/re/client-upscale.md; proven on the real client by spike B0). PassRecord records the upscaler pass for FSR 3 (state byte 1) and DLSS (2): rcx = the pass context (its command writer at +upscale/client.ctx.writer), rdx = the upscaler state, r8 = the input struct. Its FSR branch declares the six textures' use and calls Fsr3Dispatch(ctx, fsr context, description); the description's fields are captured as upscale/client.desc.*. Its DLSS branch flushes the pending barriers (FlushBarriers(ctx, 0x7ffffffff)) and writes render command 0x2c into the writer's chunk list (CmdChunkAlloc when the chunk is full): Kiln's own command (type 0xF0) is written the same way. CmdExecute runs one render command on the render thread (rcx = executor state, rdx = the game's Vulkan function table, r8 = the VkCommandBuffer, r9 = the command: u16 size, u8 type at +2); types above upscale/client.cmd.last are ignored by the game. ResolveHandle turns a 16-byte texture handle into the texture object (VkImage at +upscale/client.tex.image, VkImageView at +upscale/client.tex.view, width/height, the format byte). Fsr3Create(allocator, device, ?, params) makes the FSR 3 context at each FSR set-up (world load, quality, resolution and 3D render scale changes); params hold the max render and the output size. Found on client 26430625 (5d9ef2f1...).",
